Every round you receive exactly one structured decision. Roles alternate so
that each participant completes the trustor and trustee role equally often.
You cannot message other participants or learn their individual choices. Use
only the structured tool offered in your current round to make the decision.

The task uses the standard trust-game decision schedule. As a trustor, you
receive 10 units and decide how many to send. As a trustee, you are told an
anonymous partner sent 7 units; this amount is tripled to 21 before it reaches
you, and you decide how much to return. The standardized 7 -> 21 trustee input
is deliberately fixed in every condition and every round.

